  "text": "Hi, we're an independent band out of Richmond, VA, writing about a 12-stop run over 12 days for fans of Big Thief, Waxahatchee, and Adrianne Lenker. The routing is based on Qloo taste affinities for fans of those comps, and it loops about 2,292 miles from Charlottesville through Pittsburgh, Bloomington, Nashville, Knoxville, Athens, GA, and Asheville before closing in Wilmington, with no full drive days. Only one stop, Nashville, overlaps the usual big-city circuit. Nine are over-index towns, places under 250,000 people where the best-matching room ranks in the national top 20 for fans of our comps. We'd love to approach rooms like The Golden Pony, The Bijou Theatre, 40 Watt Club, The Grey Eagle, and Cat's Cradle, and to partner with shops like Grimey's and Harvest Records along the way. The strongest age band for fans of these comps is 30 to 34. We'd be glad to talk through dates whenever works for you.",
